  "question": {
    "text": "The sum of all rational terms in the expansion of $\\left(1+2^{1 / 3}+3^{1 / 2}\\right)^6$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "612",
  "solution": {
    "text": "The general term of multinomial expansion is\n$\\frac{6!}{\\alpha!\\beta!\\gamma!}(1)^\\alpha\\left(2^{\\frac{1}{3}}\\right)^\\beta\\left(3^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)^\\gamma$\n\nFor terms to be rational $3 \\mid \\beta$ and $2 \\mid \\gamma$\n$\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c}\n\\beta & \\gamma & \\alpha & \\text { Term } \\\\\n\\hline 0 & 0 & 6 & 1 \\\\\n0 & 2 & 4 & 15.3=45 \\\\\n0 & 4 & 2 & 15.3^2=135 \\\\\n0 & 6 & 0 & 1.3^3=27 \\\\\n3 & 0 & 3 & 20.2=40 \\\\\n3 & 2 & 1 & 60.2 .3=360 \\\\\n6 & 0 & 0 & 1.4=4\n\\end{array}$\n$\\Rightarrow$ Sum of rational terms\n$=1+45+135+27+40+360+4=612$",
    "image": null
  },
